# Landmark runs (baselines future work forks from) are kept in-repo via git-lfs.
!checkpoints/resilient-resonance-682/
*.zip
*.log
data/
outputs/
*.egg-info/
/models/
# /runs/
.agent/
wandb/
.venv/
/tmp/
.env
.claude/settings.local.json
gameplay_clips/
# Durable artifacts without an owning run, and disposable scratch output.
/artifacts/
/out/
# Recomputable machine state, not an artifact.
.vram.json
# An artifact payload is verified as a whole: `verify_artifact` requires every
# file `artifact.json` records, so a payload file the repository refuses to
# track makes a clean checkout unable to verify — or publish — anything citing
# it. The broad rules above (`*.log`, `*.zip`, `data/`) are aimed at stray local
# output and have no business reaching inside a promoted run's artifacts, so
# those payloads are re-included here. `samples/` below deliberately follows,
# and still wins: raw samples are the one payload that stays local by design.
!checkpoints/*/artifacts/**
# Raw analysis samples stay local. This rule follows the landmark whitelist
# above deliberately: a promoted run directory re-includes everything under it,
# so `samples/` has to be excluded again afterwards or a multi-gigabyte payload
# would become trackable inside checkpoints/resilient-resonance-682/.
samples/
